0\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000 Inglewood, California\rJanuary 14, 2020\r\r The City Council of the City of Inglewood, California held a regular meeting on Tuesday, January 14, 2020, in the Council Chambers in City Hall of said City.\r \r Following the Pledge of Allegiance to the flag of our Country, Mayor Butts called the City Council into joint session with the Successor Agency, Housing Authority, Finance Authority, Parking Authority, and Joint Powers Authority at the hour of 2:00 p.m.\r\r The City Clerk/Successor Agency Secretary/Housing Authority Secretary/Finance Authority Secretary/Parking Authority Secretary/Joint Powers Authority Secretary announced the presence of a quorum as follows: \r\rPresent: Mayor/Successor Agency Chairman/Housing Authority Chairman/Finance Authority Chairman/Parking Authority Chairman/Joint Powers Authority Chairman Butts, Council Members/Successor Agency Members/Housing Authority Members/Finance Authority Members/Parking Authority Members/Joint Powers Authority Members Dotson, Padilla, Morales, and Franklin; and\rAbsent: None.\r \r City/Successor Agency / Housing Authority / Finance Authority / Parking Authority /Joint Powers Authority officials and personnel present were as follows: \r\r Yvonne Horton City Clerk/Secretary*\r Artie Fields City Manager/Executive Director*\r Ken Campos City Attorney/General Counsel*\r David Esparza Asst. City Manager/CFO\r Aisha Thompson Deputy City Clerk \r\r * Serves as indicated for the Successor Agency, Housing Authority, Finance Authority, Parking Authority, and Joint Powers Authority.\r \r PUBLIC COMMENTS � AGENDA ITEMS. Mayor/Successor Agency Chairman/Housing Authority Chairman/Finance Authority Chairman/Parking Authority Chairman/Joint Powers Authority Chairman Butts inquired if there were any persons present who wished to address the City Council/Successor Agency/Housing Authority/Finance Authority/Parking Authority/Joint Powers Authority on any item on the Agenda. \r\r There was no response.\r\r142.9 PAYMENT OF WARRANTS AND BILLS. It was moved by Council Member /Successor Agency Member / Housing Authority Member Franklin, and seconded by Council Member /Successor Agency Member / Housing Authority Member Morales that the demands presented to the City Council/Successor Agency/Housing Authority dated January 9, 2020, in the amount of $2,910,302.22, are hereby allowed, and the City Clerk/Successor Agency Secretary/Housing Authority Secretary is hereby authorized to certify upon said registers that said demands are so approved. The motion was carried by the following roll call vote:\r Ayes: Council Members/Successor Agency Members/Housing Authority Members Dotson, Padilla, Morales, Franklin and Mayor/Successor Agency Chairman/Housing Authority Chairman Butts; and\rNoes: None. \r\r\r132 CLAIMS DENIED. Letters from the Office of the City Attorney recommending the following:\r A. Rejection of the following claim filed pursuant to Government Code Section 913:\r 1) Jose Benavidez for alleged vehicle damage on November 16, 2019.\r 2) Steven Hester for alleged vehicle damage on October 27, 2019.\r 3) Oscar Mercado for water shut off on November 21, 2019.\r 4) Alexandra Rodriguez for alleged property damage, and personal injury on \r May22, 2019.\r\r B. Return of the following late claim filed pursuant to Government Code Section 911.2:\r 1) Amber Winn for alleged property damage on February 8, 2019. \r \r It was moved by Council Member Morales, seconded by Council Member Franklin, that the City Council does hereby: 1) Reject the claims listed as A1-A4; and 2) Return the late claim listed as B1. The motion was carried by the following roll call vote:\r Ayes: Council Members Dotson, Padilla, Morales, Franklin, and Mayor Butts; and\r Noes: None. \r\r MINUTES. It was moved by Council Member Morales and seconded by Council Member Franklin that the Minutes for the City Council Meetings held on December 10, 2019, and December 17, 2019, be approved. The motion was carried by the following roll call vote:\r Ayes: Council Members Dotson, Padilla, Morales, Franklin and Mayor Butts; and\r Noes: None.\r\r171 CITY SPONSORSHIP APPROVED - HEALTHY AGING HEALTH FAIR. Staff report dated January 14, 2020, was presented recommending approval of City sponsorship of the Healthy Aging Health Fair for Seniors. \r \rIt was moved by Council Member Morales, and seconded by Council Member Franklin that the City Council does hereby approve City sponsorship at a cost not to exceed $3,000. The motion was carried by the following roll call vote:\rAyes: Council Members Dotson, Padilla, Morales, Franklin and Mayor Butts; and\rNoes: None.\r\r \r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r 171 RESOLUTION NO. 20-34 ADOPTED � AMENDING THE FISCAL YEAR 2019-2020 BUDGET; CONTRACT AWARDED AND AGREEMEMENT NO. 20-097 APPROVED � ABC BUILDERS, INC. Staff report dated January 14, 2020, was presented recommending award of contract and approval of an agreement for the Rogers Park Restroom Project Phase 1, per Bid No. CB-19-14, pending submission of the Fiscal Year 2019-2020 CIP Budget amendment.\r\r It was moved by Council Member Morales, and seconded by Council Member Franklin that the City Council does hereby: 1) Adopt Resolution No. 20-34 entitled:\r\r A RESOLUTION OF THE CITY COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF INGLEWOOD, CALIFORNIA, AMENDING THE 2019-20 ANNUAL BUDGET TO COVER THE EXPENDITURES FOR THE PARK RESTROOM IMPROVEMENT PROJECT PHASE 1 � ROGER PARK\r\r and 2) Award contract and approve Agreement No. 20-097 with ABC Builders, Inc., in an amount of $594,358 (includes a 10% contingency of $80,000). The motion was carried by the following roll call vote:\rAyes: Council Members Dotson, Padilla, Morales, Franklin and Mayor Butts; and\rNoes: None.\r\r 171 RESOLUTION NO. 20-35 ADOPTED � AMENDING THE FISCAL YEAR 2019-2020 BUDGET; AGREEMENT NO. 20-096 APPROVED � MDJ MANAGEMENT, LLC. Staff report dated January 14, 2020 was presented recommending approval of a cooperative service agreement with MDJ Management, LLC for resurfacing of two swimming pools at Edward Vincent, Jr., Park in accordance with the Sourcewell cooperative agreement, pending the submission of the Fiscal Year 2019-2020 CIP Budget amendment.\r\r It was moved by Council Member Morales, and seconded by Council Member Franklin that the City Council does hereby: 1) Adopt Resolution No. 20-35 entitled:\r\r A RESOLUTION OF THE CITY COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF INGLEWOOD, CALIFORNIA, AMENDING THE 2019-20 ANNUAL BUDGET TO COVER EXPENDITURES FOR THE VINCENT PARK SWIMMING POOL RESURFACING PROJECT \r\r and; 2) Approve Agreement No. 20-096 with MDJ Management, LLC, in the amount of $359,817. The motion was carried by the following roll call vote: \rAyes: Council Members Dotson, Padilla, Morales, Franklin and Mayor Butts; and\rNoes: None.\r \r171 AGREEMENT NO. 20-098 APPROVED � BETTER 4 YOU BREAKFAST, INC., DBA BETTER 4 YOU MEALS. Staff report dated January 14, 2020, was presented recommending approval of an agreement (with the option to extend three additional one year terms) with Better 4 You Breakfast, Inc., dba Better 4 You Meals, for the provision of breakfast, lunch, and snacks for the Child and Adult Care Food Program (CACFP) and Summer Food Service Program (SFSP) through August 31, 2020.\r\r It was moved by Council Member Morales, and seconded by Council Member Franklin that the City Council does hereby approve Agreement No. 20-098 in the amount of $321,757.60 The motion was carried by the following roll call vote: Ayes: Council Members Dotson, Padilla, Morales, Franklin and Mayor Butts; \r and \r Noes: None.\r\r\r 178 AGREEMENT NO. 20-099 APPROVED � BOARD OF STATE AND COMMUNITY CORRECTIONS; RESOLUTION NO. 20-36 ADOPTED � AMENDING THE 2019-2020 FISCAL YEAR BUDGET. Staff report dated January 14, 2020, was presented recommending approval of an agreement with the Board of State and Community Corrections to accept grant funds in the amount of $2,970.\r\rIt was moved by Council Member Morales, and seconded by Council Member Franklin that the City Council does hereby: 1) Approve Agreement No. 20-99 with the Board of State and Community Corrections; and 2) Adopt Resolution No. 20-36 entitled:\rA RESOLUTION OF THE CITY COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF INGLEWOOD, CALIFORNIA ACCEPTING GRANT FUNDS FROM THE BOARD OF STATE AND COMMUNITY CORRECTIONS IN THE AMOUNT OF $2,970 AND AMENDING THE FISCAL YEAR 2019-2020 ANNUAL BUDGET \r The motion was carried by the following roll call vote: \rAyes: Council Members Dotson, Padilla, Morales, Franklin and Mayor Butts; and\rNoes: None. \r \r\r 178 PAYMENT OF INVOICES APPROVED � QUEST DIAGNOSTICS. Staff report dated January 14, 2020, was presented recommending approval to pay invoices from Quest Diagnostics to perform analysis on drug test samples. \r\r It was moved by Council Member Morales, and seconded by Council Member Franklin that the City Council does hereby approve payment in the amount of $2,685.40. The motion was carried by the following roll call vote:\r Ayes: Council Members Dotson, Padilla, Morales, Franklin and Mayor Butts; and \r Noes: None.\r\r178 AGREEMENT NO. 20-100 APPROVED � CDW-G. Staff report dated January 14, 2020, was presented recommending approval of an agreement to authorize issuing a purchase order to CDW�G to provide twenty-four (24) Panasonic Toughbooks and related items to be used by the Police Department as in-car mobile data computers.\r\r It was moved by Council Member Morales, and seconded by Council Member Franklin that the City Council does hereby approve Agreement No. 20-100 not to exceed $97,356. The motion was carried by the following roll call vote:\r Ayes: Council Members Dotson, Padilla, Morales, Franklin and Mayor Butts; and \r Noes: None.\r\r178 AGREEMENT NO. 20-101 APPROVED � CNC TECHNOLOGIES, LLC. Staff report dated January 14, 2020, was presented recommending approval of an agreement with CNC Technologies, LLC to provide a video downlink and related services.\r\r It was moved by Council Member Morales, and seconded by Council Member Franklin that the City Council does hereby approve Agreement No. 20-101 in the amount of $145,120.50. The motion was carried by the following roll call vote:\r Ayes: Council Members Dotson, Padilla, Morales, Franklin and Mayor Butts; and \r Noes: None.\r\r\r125 AMENDMENT NO. 2 TO AGREEMENT NO. 18-118 APPROVED � MILLER BARONDESS, LLP. Staff report dated January 14, 2020, was presented recommending approval of Amendment No. 2 to Agreement No. 18-118 with Miller Barondess, LLP for broad ranging legal advice, guidance and representation to increase the hourly rate for attorney services from $550/hour to $650/hour, paralegal services from $150/hour to $250/hour, and add a �most favored nation� clause.\r\r It was moved by Council Member/Successor Agency Member/Parking Authority Member Morales, and seconded by Council Member/Successor Agency Member/Parking Authority Member Dotson that the City Council/Successor Agency/Parking Authority does hereby approve Amendment No. 2 to Agreement No. 18-118 with Miller Barondess, LLP. The motion was carried by the following roll call vote:\r Ayes: Council Members/Successor Agency Members/Parking Authority Members Dotson, Padilla, Morales, Franklin, and Mayor/Successor Agency Chairman/Parking Authority Chairman Butts; and \r Noes: None. \r\r 301 PUBLIC HEARING HELD � ORDINANCE NO. 20-06 INTRODUCED � APPROVING ZONING CODE AMENDMENT 2019-002 (ZCA 2019-002) TO CHAPTER 12 OF THE INGLEWOOD MUNICIPAL CODE. The City Clerk announced the next scheduled matter is a public hearing to consider an ordinance approving Zoning Code Amendment 2019-002 (ZCA 2019-002) to Chapter 12 (Planning and Zoning) of the Inglewood Municipal Code to modify regulations of the Medical Enterprise Overlay Zone citywide, that notice has been given in the time forma and manner as required by law, and that no communications were received. \r\r Artie Fields, City Manager, presented the Staff Report dated January 14, 2020.\r\r Fred Jackson, Senior Planner, gave a brief oral report. \r\r Mayor Butts inquired if there were any persons present that wished to address the City Council on this matter. \r\r There was no response. \r\r Following discussion, it was moved by Council Member Morales, and seconded by Council Member Franklin that the City Council does hereby affirm Categorical Exemption (EA-CE-2019-077). The motion was carried by the following roll call vote:\r Ayes: Council Members Dotson, Padilla, Morales, Franklin and Mayor Butts; and \r Noes: None.\r\r Thereupon, it was moved by Mayor Butts, and seconded by Council Member Morales that further reading be waived. The motion was carried by the following roll call vote:\r Ayes: Council Members Dotson, Padilla, Morales, Franklin and Mayor Butts; and \r Noes: None.\r\r Whereupon, Ordinance No. 20-06 entitled: \r\r AN ORDINANCE OF THE CITY COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF INGLEWOOD, CALIFORNIA, TO APPROVE ZONING CODE AMENDMENT 2019-002 (ZCA-2019-002) TO MODIFY REGULATIONS OF THE MEDICAL ENTERPRISE OVERLAY ZONE CITYWIDE \r\r was introduced by Council Member Morales. \r \r PUBLIC REMARKS. Mayor Butts inquired if there were any persons present who wished to address the City Council on any matter connected with City business not elsewhere considered on the Agenda. \r\r There was no response. \r\r There being no further business to be presented, Mayor Butts declared the meeting adjourned in memory of Roland Johnson, 30 year resident, and Arrick �Dobby� Turner, employee of the City of Inglewood for over 30 years, at the hour of 2:23 p.m.\r\r Mayor Butts called the City Council back in session at the hour of 2:23 p.m. \r\r114.11 APPOINTMENT TO THE PLANNING COMMISSION � RATIFIED. Upon recommendation of Council Member Dotson, It was moved by Mayor Butts, and seconded by Council Member Morales that Patricia Patrick be appointed to the Planning Commission for the term ending March 2022. The motion was carried by the following roll call vote:\r Ayes: Council Members Dotson, Padilla, Morales, Franklin and Mayor Butts;\r Noes: None.\r\r114.9 APPOINTMENT TO THE PARKS AND RECREATION COMMISSION � RATIFIED. Upon recommendation of Council Member Dotson, It was moved by Mayor Butts, and seconded by Council Member Morales that Lee Denmon be appointed to the Parks and Recreation Commission for the term ending March 2022. The motion was carried by the following roll call vote:\r Ayes: Council Members Dotson, Padilla, Morales, Franklin and Mayor Butts; and \r Noes: None.\r\r There being no further business to be presented, Mayor Butts declared the meeting adjourned at the hour of 2:24 p.m. \r\r\r Approved this 28th day of January, 2020\r\r\r_________________________\rYvonne Horton, City Clerk\r\r\r ________________________\r James Butts, Jr., Mayor\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\rJanuary 14, 2020\r\r\r\r\u0013 PAGE \\* MERGEFORMAT \u00146\u0015\r\r\r\u0013 PAGE \\* MERGEFORMAT \u00141\u0015\r\r\r\r\r\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000